script = ExtResource("1_715sv")
dialogue_id = "mq_4_40_doubts"
record_title = "Era 四: Doubts"
text = "PAGE: avatar_adult(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY)
avatar_adult: Father, do you have a moment?
avatar_adult: My heart feels clouded today.
scribe: Always, Your Holiness.
scribe: You look as though you are carrying the weight of ten shards on your shoulders.
avatar_adult: It's just...
avatar_adult: Back home, everything felt so obvious.
avatar_adult: Now, seeing so many people...
avatar_adult: So many different voices...
avatar_adult: How can I possibly make every one of them happy?
scribe: It is a difficult task, Your Holiness.
scribe: That is why we need one steady voice to unite us.
avatar_adult: But what if my voice isn't steady?
avatar_adult: I search my heart for wisdom, but all I find is doubt.
avatar_adult: I haven't had a glimpse of the Enlightened One's memory in years.
scribe: Your Holiness, when a leader stops questioning if they are right, they become a tyrant.
scribe: The fact that you hesitate before this great responsibility is proof of divine wisdom.
avatar_adult: But maybe we could start small?
avatar_adult: What if I just traveled the shards, spoke to each town directly?
scribe: It is a very kind thought.
scribe: But the Cloud Sea is vast, and people are stubborn.
scribe: They may nod along at a lone sage, then return to their habits the moment you step back through the gate.
avatar_adult: I don't know if I feel ready...
avatar_adult: Father, let me try to read the commandments again.
scribe: Here. I wish we could understand them better...
avatar_adult: ...
avatar_adult: I was hoping the divine spirit would resonate with them somehow, now that we're here...
avatar_adult: Make me remember...
scribe: You shouldn't blame yourself, Your Holiness.
scribe: The commandments were written down by ordinary people, after all, in the language of their time.
scribe: Forget these dusty old scrolls.
scribe: I have more faith in the wisdom of your heart.
avatar_adult: Thank you, Father.
avatar_adult: Your support has always meant so much to me."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
